Implement LTX-2.3 base model import

Every .ltx2_3 arm of ModelImporter is a fatalError. This adds the inspect()
detection arm and fills the seven switch arms with the working wiring from
LoRAImporter, plus the prefix-strip loop, the bare-named connector register
writes that UNetFixedEncoder reads back, a 5746-tensor write check, and an
inferModelSpecification arm mirroring the built-in zoo entry. The four
aggregate_embed mappings carry isBF16 because the text feature extractor runs
BF16 at inference and ccv_nnc_tensor_read has no 16F to 16BF path.

It also fixes a latent bug in the LTX2.swift mappers. The q and k RMSNorm
gain vectors must be row-interleaved exactly like their sibling to_q and to_k
projections, for the NNC cmul rotary pair layout, and all fourteen are mapped
plain. LoRA import never carries norm gains, so nothing exercised it.
Un-interleaved gains produce spatially fine but temporally frozen video with
a washed-out cast.
